# ─── client/.env.example ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file is COMMITTED to version control as a template.
# Copy it to client/.env and adjust values for your environment.
#
#   cp client/.env.example client/.env
#
# NEVER commit client/.env
#
# IMPORTANT: All client-side env vars MUST be prefixed with VITE_
# Vite strips all env vars that don't have the VITE_ prefix before
# bundling — non-prefixed vars are never exposed to browser code.
#
# SECURITY: Never put secrets here. These values are embedded into the
# JavaScript bundle and visible to anyone who opens DevTools.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── API URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The base URL of the Express API server.
#
# In development: the Vite proxy in vite.config.ts forwards all /api/* requests
# to http://localhost:5000 automatically, so VITE_API_URL is typically not used
# in dev. It becomes important in production when the frontend and backend are
# deployed to different domains.
#
# In production: set this to your deployed API URL, e.g. https://api.yourdomain.com
#
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
